# What builds b3sum's Linux release binaries, each line a name and a
# version: tools/b3sum-release.sh stops on another compiler or C library. The same source,
# these, and the script's fixed build directory give the same bytes on
# any machine, so anyone can rebuild a release's binary and compare
# (CONTRIBUTING.md, "Every artifact is a clean build of the version
# commit"). libc6-dev is Ubuntu 26.04's: the static binary holds its
# code. A commit changes a line; no release is built on a newer one first.
# apt-snapshot is the day of Ubuntu's archive that has that libc6-dev
# (snapshot.ubuntu.com): tools/b3sum-release-container.sh installs from it.
rustc 1.99.1
libc6-dev 2.43-2ubuntu2.7
apt-snapshot 20261116T000000Z
# image is the container the build runs in, by its digest (the one for
# both architectures): the commands in CONTRIBUTING.md and b3sum/README.md
# and the workflows read it from this line, so a rebuild anywhere starts
# from the bytes GitHub's machines start from.
image ubuntu:26.04@sha256:d66b366dac61b575bee2aef07e9c26e8070096fbe84a3d4d3eb0da069b5d76db
